  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Fanuc post and the Doosan DNM post wrote the stream's pose letters as the `A` and `B` words under `G43.4`.\nThe pose law is `axis = Ry(B)·Rx(A)·Z` (`crates/cl/src/cl/pose.rs`).\nOn the tilt head (`assets/machines/tilthead.mch`), the A rotary carries the B rotary, so the machine reads the words as `Rx(A)·Ry(B)·Z`.\nWhen A and B both turn, that is a different tool axis. The check did not see it.\n\nThis PR makes the posted words the joint angles of the machine's own chain:\n\n- `crates/post/src/post/tilt_chain.rs` (new): a prelude function `chainAngles(p)` that every post script sees. It reads the nest of the A rotary (about X) and the B rotary (about Y) from `machine.rotaries` (`parent`, `turnsPart`) and solves the joint angles when A is the outer factor.\n- `crates/post/src/machine/tilt_chain.rs` (new): the same rule in Rust, `joint_angles(machine, letters)`.\n- `crates/post/src/machine/judge.rs`: `pose_problems` judges the joint angles against the travel, not the letters. The check and the post read the same angles.\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`, `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`: `tilt()` calls `chainAngles` and writes its angles back on the record, so the feed cap and the held angles use them too.\n\nThe rule:\n\n- A pose that turns at most one of A and B keeps its letters exactly (the two products are then the same rotation).\n- The outer factor is the parent rotary in a head chain, the rotary nearest the work in a table chain, and the table in a table-and-head machine. B outer: the letters. A outer: solved again.\n- Away from B = 90 deg there are two solutions. The first one that both travels hold is used, else the principal one (B in -90..90). The travel check then refuses it by name.\n\nRefused by name, in the post and in the check, with the same text:\n\n- A and B both turn and the machine does not state which rotary carries the other.\n- A rotary of the A-and-B pair is stated along -X or -Y and turns.\n- C turns as well on a chain where A is the outer rotary.\n\nOther posts: I searched every post in `assets/posts/` for the same pass-through. Only `fanuc.cps` and `doosan-dnm.cps` write stream A and B words under RTCP. `mach4.cps` solves its own AC trunnion. `tormach.cps` has a lone A. `linuxcnc`, `richauto`, `sinumerik-810m` and `heidenhain-klartext` refuse tilted moves. Only `tilthead.mch` has two tilting rotaries in `assets/machines/`.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/4417-tilt-chain-joint-angles.md`.\n\n## Changed recorded programs (one by one)\n\nEach change is the old wrong axis replaced by the joint angles. I checked each by hand with `Rx(A)·Ry(B)·Z`.\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/multiaxis_deburr_tilthead.nc`: `A16.78 B-47.983` -> `A24.251 B-45.342`, `A16.78 B47.983` -> `A24.251 B45.342`. The lone `A-16.78` of the two other corners becomes `A-24.251` (B stays modal, the same value).\n- `examples/catalog/multiaxis/indexed/indexed.nc`: the Tilted pocket `A30. B30.` -> `A33.69 B25.659`. The `.camproj` did not change (the rebuild bumped only its version field, from main's format; I did not commit that).\n- Test expectations: `vendor_mch_cli` (`A30 B15` -> `A30.867 B12.953`), `program_units` (`A-45 B12.25` -> `A-45.66 B8.629`), `example_catalog` (`catalog_multiaxis_indexed::posts_two_single_axis_indexes_and_one_tilted_pocket` reads the posted joint angles).\n- `setup_align_multiaxis`: its hand-built bench machine stated no nest, so the check now refuses its poses. The bench now states \"B carries A\" (the pose law's own nest). Its programs do not change.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/post/tests/tilt_chain_joints.rs` (new):\n\n- `fanuc_posts_the_joint_angles_of_a_chain_where_a_carries_b` and `doosan_dnm_posts_the_joint_angles_of_a_chain_where_a_carries_b`: post poses with A and B not zero on `tilthead.mch`. The forward kinematics of the posted words equals the stream axis within 1e-4. The check's `joint_angles` equals the posted words.\n- `a_chain_where_b_carries_a_posts_the_pose_letters`: the same poses on the swapped nest post the letters, and the axes agree.\n- `a_chain_with_no_stated_nest_is_refused_by_name`\n- `the_machine_check_judges_the_joint_angles_not_the_letters`\n- `a_pose_past_ninety_takes_the_second_solution_inside_the_travel`\n\nRed first: with the posts of main (`git checkout 392980120 -- assets/posts/fanuc.cps assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`), the three post tests fail (log `gate-4417-eae2d557a-red.log`).\n\n## Gate (final head c91e47da3, Mac lane, `--pool`)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 852 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. This includes the example catalog suites `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test tilt_chain_joints`: 6 passed.\n- Tilt-head users outside the quick plan: `rotary_verify`, `post_not_judged`, `setup_align_multiaxis`, `mcp_multiaxis_deburr_post`, `folder_lists`: all passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- Targeted heavy step (P1, safety floor): `cargo xtask gate heavy --only \"app heavy: example_catalog\"`: 1 step, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A table-table A/B chain and a table-and-head A/B machine: the rule covers them, but no shipped machine has one, and no test posts on one.\n- `sign_convention: \"table_rh\"` on a rotary: these posts ignore it, as before. Filed as #4436 (P1).\n- The machine model pose (`crates/sim/src/machine_model/pose.rs`) takes explicit joint values. I did not check which caller feeds it stream letters.\n- The catalog case `multiaxis/five-axis` (PR #4408) is not on main. It must be rebuilt after this merges.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts write the joint angles of the machine's A/B tilt chain under G43.4 (a tilt head whose A carries B no longer reads a different tool axis); the machine check judges the same angles, and a chain whose nest is not stated is refused by name.\n\nFixes #4417\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
